  "summary": "Seven preprints from 9-16 November pair AI structure predictors and generative models with enhanced sampling and MD to resolve ensembles, not single folds.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is a move from single predicted structures to conformational ensembles that are checked or generated with physical sampling. Several preprints couple AI predictors or generative models to MD-based validation: REVEAL links secondary-structure sampling, trRosettaRNA2, unbiased MD and Markov state modeling for HIV-1 TAR RNA, and bAIes is extended to six predictors for disordered-protein ensembles. Others use enhanced sampling (funnel-restrained TAMD with beta-VAE clustering for CYFIP1-eIF4E; OneOPES for FCP1 binding Rap74) to resolve multimodal binding landscapes. New elements include OriDynamics as a unified all-atom ensemble generator, a transition-conditioned dynamical fingerprint for rare events, and ProtFlap, which predicts residue flexibility from static structures using atomic energy features.",
